{"title":"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/1/ea14332ec5352ee40a2cb8f208326bc25f4ed95c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" /> is equal to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/8/a28d13614a1eb8cf22b9b847e115d5a8354ebd6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ \\frac{1}{6} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ \\frac{1}{5} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ \\frac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"408\" height=\"38\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can first find the least common denominator, convert each fraction, and then add them.\n</p><p>We can see that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are coprime (i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />'s greatest common factor is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />), because both are prime numbers. This means the least common denominator will just be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/6/7665cc4223d31e60fba93de9e8e901b3bd737b3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 3 = 6$\" width=\"73\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Converting these, we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bf9ac0546212f6d722ea5665a8a4432d2543b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{1 \\times 3}{2 \\times 3} = \\frac{3}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"121\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/d/98d1309fb83c7bb510c62ebc4d275ca6d3140a88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{1 \\times 2}{3 \\times 2} = \\frac{2}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"121\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Adding these together, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afaa5a3481a67351cd0095f4ee65c22431f69cac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{6} + \\frac{2}{6} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } \\frac{5}{6}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"133\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(answer_choices)\">Solution 2 (answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The answer must be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192b4a258ee998961a99523fd0f0a029f9ea194a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.5$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192b4a258ee998961a99523fd0f0a029f9ea194a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.5$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/a/01aab4e2acc0de0ee4ea6fd1771b1c8898504920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3} &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" />. However, we also know that it is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c0a9dea63b933465e96b728da1546fb1ce3baa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3} &lt; \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{2}{2} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"193\" height=\"38\" /> due to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> having a larger denominator than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43bf1b8c99758eddc23a8f2e1c9ab71995f16587.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5} = 0.4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"38\" />, which is less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192b4a258ee998961a99523fd0f0a029f9ea194a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.5$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />, so answer choice A is incorrect. This also eliminates answer choices B and C because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/3/e23f2c998afde6dc46fabc4f444cbf84fbf1d9fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6} &lt; \\frac{1}{5} &lt; \\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" /> for similar logic and the numerator being larger in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2297526ede0e6c616802ca72adf69c82518f25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> than in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d129a7b3c0bf9fbd0693afdd426a66d2a0a8c3ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/2/7821f1bc9b8d5558ae5725bbcebb996aae15cd2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{2} &gt; \\frac{2}{2} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"86\" height=\"38\" />. However, we know that the result must be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so answer choice D is eliminated (we could have also seen that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/0/bc0342a4ac8548665d39b0c99f5d75f77e4c5fce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{2} = 1.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"37\" />)\n</p><p>Since all of the other answer choices have been eliminated, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/7/eb7b9769d590c7393f90a266bbee61da9de42fdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } \\frac{5}{6}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"60\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/inde